WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.088 --> 00:00:05.388
We built AI Radar because finding a paper and understanding it are two different

2
00:00:05.388 --> 00:00:06.088
challenges.

3
00:00:06.475 --> 00:00:11.562
Researchers need to keep up, while students entering a new field can feel lost

4
00:00:11.562 --> 00:00:12.575
in technical language.

5
00:00:12.988 --> 00:00:14.775
We wanted to make that first step easier.

6
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.938
The homepage keeps things simple: a central search box, saved category shortcuts,

7
00:00:21.162 --> 00:00:22.838
and monthly submission rankings.

8
00:00:23.225 --> 00:00:26.462
Deep reading and language settings are available at the top.

9
00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:31.029
Search an official arXiv category by name or code.

10
00:00:31.492 --> 00:00:36.454
For example, C S dot A I takes us straight to artificial intelligence.

11
00:00:37.254 --> 00:00:43.317
Selecting a category retrieves up to five recent papers and generates an overview.

12
00:00:43.729 --> 00:00:48.329
Here, we're opening a saved report, starting with the shared research context.

13
00:00:49.142 --> 00:00:53.567
Each paper pairs a plain language explanation with a concrete illustration.

14
00:00:53.967 --> 00:00:57.904
This example shows an agent learning to avoid tools that have stopped working.

15
00:00:58.671 --> 00:01:03.858
Expand a card to explore the problem, approach, results, and limitations.

16
00:01:04.258 --> 00:01:08.621
The illustrations explain concepts; they aren't experimental results.

17
00:01:09.433 --> 00:01:11.195
Start with a saved frontier overview.

18
00:01:11.608 --> 00:01:15.395
The top-level deep-reading button opens a compact paper list.

19
00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:18.833
Select one paper, or add another for joint reading.

20
00:01:19.233 --> 00:01:24.221
Opening the collection brings those papers and their PDFs into the reading workspace.

21
00:01:29.516 --> 00:01:31.504
The collection stays editable.

22
00:01:31.904 --> 00:01:36.804
Removing one paper changes the workspace from joint reading to single-paper reading.

23
00:01:37.216 --> 00:01:40.679
New generation starts only when you press Generate report.

24
00:01:41.558 --> 00:01:46.871
Now we switch to a separate saved two-paper report, not a newly generated result.

25
00:01:48.558 --> 00:01:54.258
This report compares two papers, keeping their identities and page counts visible.

26
00:01:54.695 --> 00:01:59.645
Follow a citation, and its original excerpt now opens immediately.

27
00:02:00.058 --> 00:02:04.821
The paper title and physical PDF page stay attached to the evidence.

28
00:02:05.208 --> 00:02:09.071
The source PDF remains available for checking important claims.

29
00:02:13.642 --> 00:02:16.154
The interface supports English and Chinese.

30
00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:21.917
Reports can be English, Chinese, or bilingual, with interface and report languages

31
00:02:21.917 --> 00:02:23.067
selected independently.

32
00:02:23.879 --> 00:02:28.992
Our biggest lesson was turning a vague idea into clear requirements, then breaking

33
00:02:28.992 --> 00:02:31.642
a large feature into manageable tasks.

34
00:02:32.029 --> 00:02:35.717
We learned through planning, building, testing, and feedback.

35
00:02:36.517 --> 00:02:42.129
We believe AI Radar deserves recognition because it connects discovery, understandable

36
00:02:42.142 --> 00:02:47.842
explanations, and traceable evidence in one workflow, helping people approach unfamiliar

37
00:02:47.854 --> 00:02:49.579
research with greater confidence.
